#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:5
#: f13e525eb3304baa95c7d9b9e5410a38
msgid "Archived: Build Your Own Multicopter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:8
#: ede68681dca34feab95bccf370995841
msgid "There are Lots of Ways you Can Put Together a MultiCopter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:10
#: fa1b36d6a1fc438d8af870d5a546fbf7
msgid ""
"Thoughtful, slow progression is better than jumping in with both feet, "
"you can easily get discouraged by trying to do too much too fast."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:13
#: 8bba91033bbf4565b8b7bef60fb0fbcf
msgid ""
"You are likely to have a good experience if you start with a simple, "
"small QuadCopter, either a Ready to Fly or an All Inclusive Kit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:15
#: 4d5a65e474614cbb9bcce849d0e011c3
msgid ""
"For those with good DIY capabilities an Almost Ready To Fly build like "
"the F450 FlameWheel described below can also work well."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:17
#: 6284151e436749d687d48a43bafb7eb6
msgid ""
"For your first MultiCopter, DO NOT initially try to build a Photo / Video"
" or First Person View copter, just build a good QuadCopter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:19
#: a97e6aaeb4d548df91a8bad0f9586355
msgid ""
"Even if you know that's what you really want to do, it will take you some"
" time to come up to speed on our copters and autopilots."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:21
#: 6b552052d894463a98d52206972380d5
msgid ""
"If you just want to get a taste and have a lot of fun, try one of the "
"little inexpensive, safe, sturdy, ready to use Micro-QuadCopters below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:24
#: c84ca58b17b54db196f0031628017947
msgid ""
"If you know you're serious, try the **Flamewheel ARF Build** or if you "
"just want to fly and can afford it get the high end \\ **Iris** "
"QuadCopter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:27
#: 7e048f837f4a4a38b736278a9b8801de
msgid ""
"The Iris includes a top end \\ **Pixhawk** autopilot and both the Iris "
"and the Flamewheel can do **FPV** or **Video** when you are ready."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:30
#: 2a8106075a2f469bb07778c6f1c1a314
msgid ""
"Don't start with a \\ **Frame Up Build** unless you have a complete "
"article on how to build a really good simple Quadcopter like the Flip "
"Sport."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:33
#: 4af00d9cbce2495ab82038a81fd3ebab
msgid ""
"Absolutely do not start by trying to **Build Your Own Frame**, even among"
" experienced builders there are more failures than successes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:35
#: c71017874f194b69880119a8db35c36d
msgid ""
"It is very important to **NOT** start out with a big (dangerous) "
"multicopter with a bunch of photo or video stuff on it, you will regret "
"it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:38
#: 3c454761cc424cd9a59b29808858df7e
msgid ""
"A small, agile **QuadCopter** is always a lot more fun to fly than a big,"
" ponderous and slow **Hex** or **OctoCopter** in any case."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:40
#: 512986c3b07c4d7e86b47e87bf6c7c77
msgid ""
"Except for top end professional HD video or photography requiring big "
"cameras you are always better off thinking small, light and agile."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:45
#: ee7e1a6ea3fe46f8843ee198d06f9f05
msgid ""
"Safety is very important with multicopters, keep plenty of distance from "
"living or expensive things and review our \\ :ref:`Safety Page <safety-"
"multicopter>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:49
#: 6b14d03a2e914fc7800a765f767a8113
msgid "Chinese Imports Good Deal / Bad Deal?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:51
#: 94e126c96792465abf29659537bdad79
msgid ""
"It is very tempting especially when just starting out to buy lots of "
"Chinese direct import stuff because it is so much cheaper: Bad Idea!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:53
#: 96993344266d4a0e9da7f1d7c281c19a
msgid ""
"As you gain experience, you will learn which import items are "
"serviceable, if you try to do it at the beginning things will not go "
"well."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:56
#: 115be8bde65e4f51b1f5e4c4379e7c02
msgid ""
"I recommend you always get the main electronics (autopilot) from the "
"primary source, in our case the Pixhawk from 3DRobotics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:58
#: 8e022becfbb0448cb25ca43a652b1a95
msgid ""
"You will also want to get the electronic accessories (GPS, magentometer, "
"telemetry and OSD if used) from 3DRobotics as well."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:60
#: 6f1237d0b76d473796ed26d3b9be051a
msgid ""
"If your going to do first person view, get a 3DRobotics FPV kit or a "
"FatShark Attitude video goggle and transmitter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:62
#: a1670fe158b14f0881923fd2b5abe47d
msgid ""
"As for cameras, the GoPro Hero 3 and especially the Black is the one to "
"get, because it is what everybody uses and it works well."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:64
#: 9d75409ea7af469eb969e8847ca58050
msgid ""
"The DJI Flamewheel ARF kit which is recommended is made in China but is a"
" known quality setup, so where you get it is up to you."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:66
#: fe687a11a18047d082c96b3864cf4def
msgid ""
"The Traxxas, Hubsan and Helimax highly recommended starter micro-"
"Quadcopters are also made in China but are still a great way to start."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:69
#: 88b7843bb9784b13b70820b9ecb4b356
msgid ""
"Motors, Batteries, ESCs, frames and even FRSky or Turnigy RC transmitters"
" and receivers can be very good deals direct from China."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:71
#: 589482e0319b4c32bb9d526ef7b5c85e
msgid ""
"A lot of items we buy domestically are actually made in China and of "
"course, quality varies widely, regardless of country of origin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:73
#: 79dea81fbaff468599d1db9b98d58aed
msgid ""
"A $25.00 RC-Timer motor is not likely to be of the same quality as the "
"equivalent $100.00 Tiger-Motor, but hey, it's only $25.00."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:75
#: d6624c3779e84d3e8721335f40b83af1
msgid ""
"Although direct Chinese imports generally have pretty reliable shipping, "
"aftermarket support or returns are often very problematic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:77
#: 8a217387fcfc426d8f7294d51e84cb74
msgid ""
"If you build in a ten to twenty percent broken, damaged or not included "
"expectation for Chinese imports you will not be disappointed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:80
#: d88ec80be501435db093e349aa30b119
msgid ""
"In any case, start with two or three of the recommended \"builds\" below "
"so that you can experience success and learn to fly first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:84
#: 4de4542f287045c691240720ccfb4c28
msgid "Inexpensive, Ready To Fly Nano, Micro or Small QuadCopter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:88
#: cdef6c71a6934fe3985fffe7289ebfb8
msgid ""
"If you are new to MultiCopters, I very strongly suggest you start with "
"one of these inexpensive Ready To Fly QuadCopters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:91
#: 64ec1903efdd4caab0176d89cb4553e2
msgid ""
"They come with everything you need including the radio and the battery, "
"require no assembly, are very sturdy and are great for learning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:94
#: 51dcb0a4253f44608045ea7eb21760b0
msgid ""
"They are also a ton of fun, can easily and safely be used indoors and "
"typically cost less than a hundred dollars."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:96
#: 2fa3f6ff00eb4551bfb4d423b5d10832
msgid ""
"Importantly you will get you a much better understanding of how they work"
" and of what you really want to do next."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:98
#: accb6b9b75e14bb0ab9e0f272a8c48a1
msgid ""
"The `Traxxas QR1 QuadCopter "
"<http://traxxas.com/products/models/heli/6208qr1>`__ is an inexpensive "
"RTF Micro Quadcopter that is great for a first experience. (Left image "
"below)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:101
#: aef41ef9dc994767be469007ef432f36
msgid ""
"For $45.00 the `(Hubsan X4) "
"<http://www.amazon.com/Hubsan-X4-H107-Copter-2-4GHZ/dp/B009M1PO7W>`__ is "
"identical to the Traxxas and for $70.00 you can get it with a still photo"
" and 720P HD video camera.\\ `Husban "
"<http://www.amazon.com/Hubsan-X4-H107-Copter-2-4GHZ/dp/B009M1PO7W>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:106
#: ecfb54ff5182461795b016f67948751b
msgid ""
"For $200.00 there is even a really easy to fly **FPV** version of the "
"`Hubsan <http://www.ebay.com/itm/like/171203630670?lpid=82\">`__ that "
"comes with a RC transmitter with an excellent LCD display."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:109
#: a844f07e17354f86a3bcee8fa742fabb
msgid ""
"Even the parts for the Hubsans are readily available: \\ `Hobby Flip "
"<http://hobbyflip.com/>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:110
#: 6c6dc81b9b574c2085eb4e1cd8954473
msgid ""
"The \\ `Helimax 1SQ <http://www.helimax-"
"rc.com/helicopters/hmxe0834-1sq/index.html>`__ is another low cost palm "
"sized micro QuadCopter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:112
#: cb10106bf81449eb96c64534ba1e06ec
msgid ""
"Or even the really, really tiny $40.00 `Estes Proto X "
"<http://www.amazon.com/Estes-4606-Proto-Nano-Quadcopter/dp/B00G924W98>`__"
" actually a Hubsan H111 which flies remarkably well (Middle and right "
"images below)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:125
#: 8593654d73ab42efba079e96665b5191
msgid ""
"Below left is a larger, but very durable copter, the $88.00 UDI U818A "
"2.4GHz Quadcopter with Camera from Amazon Prime."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:127
#: 903a4b61dd4d4dffa6f84774f3da5b51
msgid ""
"And a link to an important `Blog Article by RocklandUSA "
"<https://diydrones.com/profiles/blogs/noob-quadcopter-training-thank-you-"
"community>`__ for all people considering their first Multicopter "
"purchase."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:129
#: 8e2173cdcb3e47ce93daf32515200527
msgid ""
"The Blade Nano QX at $90.00 below right is also highly recommended, is "
"very light and easy to fly and incredibly durable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:138
#: 81cd227f4bfa42e8ae3db22581f9ddcb
msgid ""
"If you are just starting out: Get one of these inexpensive, small, "
"durable Quadcopters and learn to fly it well, it will save you a lot of "
"money."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:143
#: 4907ca5a2311437eae102916348af493
msgid "All Inclusive Kit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:145
#: de68dd01dbc74dac89eef7d604eadcd1
msgid ""
"#. The easiest way to build is to buy a single kit that has all the parts"
" necessary in one box and a set of instructions for each step."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:148
#: 71e2a627e2da4ceb85c61ba7be5e60a0
msgid ""
"#. Outside of (Ready To Fly) a good all inclusive kit is the most "
"reliable and straightforward way to construct a quality MultiCopter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:151
#: a630fd85fc1445cda3cc4c337dac4da5
msgid ""
"#. Usually all of the components are well balanced with each other and "
"the entire craft can be expected to perform well."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:154
#: 7778b05f98224ba391735139f9d115c0
msgid ""
"#. For an all inclusive kit, assembly is just nuts and bolts and possibly"
" some soldering."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:157
#: a7b0fa20ac574fab9b9378e08fbe0fa6
msgid ""
"#. The assembly procedure is usually well explained in the supplied "
"instructions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:160
#: 9b88990be3444bc3a9fd951da8ad7123
msgid ""
"#. The downside is that often quality kits are a bit more expensive than "
"other alternatives and customization has to be added on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:163
#: c9065d6a7e99428d8f612fe95dfbc8a9
msgid ""
"#. If you are not already well qualified at Do It Yourself projects, A "
"good all inclusive kit is definitely the best place to start."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:166
#: 079a245bbfab4c279bf002f2df6f96db
msgid ""
"#. The innovative `Iris QuadCopter <https://www.amazon.com/3DRobotics-"
"3DR0171-3DR-IRIS-Quadcopter/dp/B00NWXY076>`__ is actually \\ **Ready To "
"Fly** and comes with the top of the line **Pixhawk** autopilot. However, "
"these are no longer produced/sold by 3DR."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:170
#: 1e64debeb29a4a8eb91e983c9a2ce663
msgid ""
"It is capable of fully autonomous flight and includes the RC transmitter,"
" the battery and even telemetry, at $750.00 it is a real bargain."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:173
#: c7bbc8f844704c6ca1a62c52fb977f1e
msgid ""
"The Iris structurally strong and resilient and it is set up to support a "
"GoPro camera or even FPV (First Person View) when you are ready."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:181
#: 55d0ca2a6427406e90f94759f4a37d58
msgid "Almost Ready to Fly"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:183
#: 768bd2ad92b2464f938cf4b071a43700
msgid ""
"If you need everything and want the most versatile copter possible you "
"can't beat the Iris above, it is simply a great deal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:185
#: 5f8299d2ccc14eafa6fba523a5e2988c
msgid ""
"If you already have a RC transmitter you can save some money and still "
"build a really high quality autonomous QuadCopter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:187
#: c47811806ccc4ed19b1369ccd087bffc
msgid "Even if you are just starting there are a few really good choices."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:189
#: 99c2db73ea004f04872284123e714c9a
msgid ""
"The **DJI F450 Flamewheel QuadCopter ARF Kit** may well be single the "
"best choice at this time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:191
#: 1b7caf1fa2cc42f2b499dab7ead7da28
msgid ""
"This kit comes with frame with built in power distribution board, the 4 "
"motors and the 4 Electronic Speed Controls and 8 Propellers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:193
#: 4462c52f4373443b803b821f14f4ea7e
msgid ""
"You need to add a :ref:`Pixhawk <common-pixhawk-overview>` Flight "
"controller, A battery and your Radio Control Transmitter and Receiver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:196
#: 821cc2d162454a038d4d01a09cb290af
msgid ""
"The supplied equipment in the kit is all first rate and the real DJI "
"Flamewheel frame is very stiff and sturdy (a good thing)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:198
#: a175f3b645004c65b0809b0802fd848b
msgid ""
"Cost: F450 ARF kit $180.00, Pixhawk with GPS/Compass $280.00 and a "
"Battery $35.00 = ($495.00) plus a PPM-Sum receiver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:201
#: 357cdfb133ff4cbeab2ceea3cc825df0
msgid ""
"As an alternative, the smaller **DJI F330 Flamewheel Quadcopter** is also"
" an excellent choice and can be better in smaller spaces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:204
#: 519fc8384a9141daa2b4d2c1a0c050ac
msgid ""
"The :ref:`Wiki page on constructing the F330 <dji-f330-flamewheel>` is "
"applicable to the **F450** as well."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:207
#: ee5127e13cdd492eba74ca5b684d6deb
msgid ""
"Most ARF kits that are cheaper than this are not nearly as sturdy and the"
" components generally fail much more frequently."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:209
#: 0cc80c3ac058418c95f7e0bf7eb5ef03
msgid ""
"You can buy the `F450 ARF kit Here! "
"<http://www.amainhobbies.com/product_info.php/cPath/2_382_2405_3233_3237/products_id/235232/n"
"/DJI-Innovations-Flame-Wheel-F450-ARF-Quadcopter-Kit-w-Motors-ESC-"
"Propellers>`__ This source has the **F350 ARF** kit also."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:211
#: d0a5460ece3f428f9ee5d62a1b5331bf
msgid ""
"DO NOT get a clone kit that looks like it, the real DJI motors and ESCs "
"are top quality and the frame is stiff and strong, the clones are not."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:214
#: d5a5f93a27204fddbe572dbab0f63cba
msgid ""
"There are more expensive high quality ARF kits available but the "
"FlameWheels will give great service and have very high performance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:216
#: eff37c41d88141d5a8ad4afed0f25ce6
msgid ""
"If you want to keep initial cost to a bare minimum, start with a `Simple "
"Flight Controller "
"<http://www.hobbyking.com/hobbyking/store/__24723__Hobbyking_KK2_0_Multi_rotor_LCD_Flight_Control_Board.html>`__"
" then graduate to a `Pixhawk <https://store.3dr.com/products/3dr-"
"pixhawk>`__ when you are ready"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:221
#: 7c2fc14e81b84f6a931ef39672cc5479
msgid ""
"The F450 can also serve as a competent Gopro and Gimbal carrying photo "
"and video copter or as an FPV platform."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:223
#: 49ba932133a340b9bb4ca9fa52d91187
msgid ""
"The **DJI F550 ARF Hexacopter** is a good choice for more advanced uses, "
"but it is not ideal as a first MultiCopter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:230
#: dd45cc9a9a534b45af4fdb1ce867f4f7
msgid "Frame Kit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:232
#: 6549162d5cdf4aca96dd3ab6502b0bcb
msgid ""
"Once you get into building your own MultiCopter based on a frame kit you "
"are getting into the big leagues, this is really not for beginners."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:235
#: 2076b76a7f714f9d8a6601b27d646be9
msgid ""
"The exception is if you are carefully following a specific and highly "
"detailed build."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:237
#: 97a2de620abc4563a2c70593de2bd0ec
msgid ""
"I am working on 2 Frame Kit based builds at the moment, a Flip 380 Sport "
"QuadCopter and a Tarot 650 Carbon Fiber Quadcopter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:239
#: b1715e567d2346aabb1ac90123d47360
msgid "A little bit on the reasons for and methods used in each of the Builds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:241
#: 2ef5148e437841cb8a53bfb3fe876cd7
msgid ""
"The Hoverthings \\ `Flip 380 Sport <http://www.hoverthings.com/the-flip-"
"black>`__ Frame is billed as the most indestructible frame ever."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:244
#: fc4e770f97524b76872ed0c2c0234583
msgid ""
"It uses incredibly stiff and strong CNC machined 1/4\" thick Fiberglass "
"arms and G10 Fiberglass center plates."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:246
#: c3cea78fe0d548c787950f962dccf3bd
msgid ""
"It can incorporate the same motors and ESCs as used in the DJI Flamewheel"
" and can use up to 10\" propellers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:248
#: a6b6c90f5c7e447298ababb81c0a8de2
msgid ""
"I purchased the Flip Sport Kit plus an extra pair of \"tab\" type center "
"sections and extra 7/8\" spacers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:250
#: 9d79f18568d74319823c8498d21de9d9
msgid ""
"The extra center plates mount below the stock plates on 7/8\" spacers to "
"accommodate the battery and flight gear."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:252
#: 69fb5f702b4242d18d990d0603c7eacf
msgid ""
"I am using 4 of the stock DJI Flamewheel motors and a special `4 in 1 ESC"
" "
"<http://mymobilemms.com/OFFTHEGRIDWATER.CA/index.php?main_page=product_info&cPath=2_4&products_id=203>`__"
" placed between the center plates of the copter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:258
#: d29a74a67a474c9bbac91032e6445b05
msgid ""
"The 4 in 1 ESC produces much less RF and DC interference and is neater "
"than 4 ESCs and a power distribution board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:260
#: d5b842f8d9064a2ba740ec2cf4d8b669
msgid ""
"I am using `GemFan DJI hub compatible 10\" carbon filled propellers "
"<http://www.rcdude.com/servlet/the-2498/GemFan-DJI-Hub-10x4.5/Detail>`__ "
"because they are very tough and very efficient."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:262
#: d114f672ed7e429f83f32058cdb398d6
msgid ""
"My goal is to build an even tougher and higher performance copter than "
"the DJI F450 Flamewheel - inexpensively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:264
#: c5714bb7577e4d9da1dff5b0077d8bf7
msgid ""
"Although it's a small copter the Flip is powerful and agile enough to use"
" FPV video and/or a GoPro Camera and brushless gimbal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:266
#: d8584ccc250046b989029360300dda72
msgid ""
"Here is a link to the :ref:`Hoverthings Flip Sport Quadcopter Wiki Build "
"Page <hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter>` using a Pixhawk autopilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:271
#: b96086063e964be3a4132b59b9b3ba9a
msgid ""
"The `Tarot 650 <http://www.ebay.com/itm/Tarot-Iron-Man-650-Foldable-3K-"
"carbon-fiber-Quad-copter-Quadcopter-Frame-TL65B02-/151050276421>`__ is a "
"carbon fiber frame that is quite large for a QuadCopter and it can "
"incorporate up to 17\" propellers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:275
#: de333b42ae8245cebc161f934be8d453
msgid ""
"I am using 360kv slow speed, large diameter \\ **Pancake Motors** "
"designed to turn the more efficient large propellers at low speeds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:278
#: d27aea02792849af91dd9ae5a4e6415c
msgid ""
"I will be using a variety of 14\" to 17\" propellers to explore "
"performance and efficiency at various propeller diameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:280
#: c488fb3e09bf4bf1854297c1b6c747bf
msgid ""
"Although the Flip Sport build shown above could be appropriate for a "
"first QuadCopter, this Tarot 650 build is definitely not."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:282
#: 3af7d8ba6897479b991ad0149cdcc7f8
msgid ""
"This quad is big enough to serve as a heavy lift or long endurance copter"
" or to carry a big video or still camera, but:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:285
#: f720d859c0584f0f992393d35cafa0d3
msgid ""
"For lifting a 2KG payload with a quadcopter you need some serious motor "
"and some serious prop."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:287
#: d3668619b9a842fa95d14b8403f5d5ea
msgid ""
"`Four Tigermotor MN4010 475 KV motors "
"<http://www.rctigermotor.com/html/2013/Navigator_0910/38.html>`__ at "
"$86.00 each, four 15 x 5 or 16 x 5 props and four high quality 30 amp "
"ESCs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:290
#: 86de71d87abc4b6284489329aa1fb17a
msgid ""
"It needs 10,000mah of 4 cell Lipo batteries (two 5000's) to achieve "
"approximately ~10 minutes of flight time at 4KG total weight."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:293
#: 77862bc2c5314716958ab6588e974577
#, python-format
msgid ""
"It should be capable of lifting 4 KG total (including 2KG payload) and "
"leave about 50% reserve thrust (minimum needed) (6kg total)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:296
#: 6233e44d87e34740b3d8224cdbe1022c
msgid ""
"You will need 16\" x 5  props to achieve the thrust and efficiency "
"necessary to lift 4KG total with reasonable flight times."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:299
#: 6f81e2f05b6e41e38f6aeea9127fb3b3
msgid ""
"That is why the bigger motors with the lower KV are required and they "
"need to be high quality to withstand continuous high output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:302
#: c5bfc4e0b8834c0b99120b3ee29b909e
msgid ""
"It is very highly recommended that you do not attempt to construct one of"
" these for your first build."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:305
#: cd9eb7e1af754bfb82a7c56d3eaf4b44
msgid ""
"A really handy link for quickly calculating performance requirements for "
"various multicopters and components: `eCalc "
"<http://www.ecalc.ch/indexcalc.htm>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:312
#: 92dffc756d2a4af2bce990ba0a8ced26
msgid ""
"**Or Perhaps a really tiny little `250 sized $10.00 frame "
"<http://www.hobbyking.com/hobbyking/store/__47075__HobbyKing_FPV250_Quad_Copter_A_Mini_Sized_FPV_Multi_Rotor_kit_.html>`__"
" with FPV capability you can fly indoors or out.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:322
#: fab135f0fbaa47e0b083705ade4cff30
msgid "Scratch Built"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:324
#: 542abb642a14465094d7f0f48087aebd
msgid ""
"Although this is often attempted by those who have never used a "
"multicopter, it very seldom turns out well."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:326
#: fc903f911f2d423585b74d738841e110
msgid ""
"At the simplest level a functioning QuadCopter can be built out of sticks"
" or dowels and plywood that will fly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:328
#: c070bff82c18436d83f3a1bb5e0297f4
msgid ""
"But it is very unlikely to fly well or to be very serviceable or to well "
"tolerate less than perfect \"landings\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:330
#: 00a470ebcd004c48a63ed8ae33248825
msgid ""
"And this is no way to save money, RTF, Kits and ARF include high quality "
"matched components and actually cost less."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:332
#: a50435eaf80e4df499032e4060162a20
msgid ""
"Even if you are an experienced model builder, machinist or engineer, DO "
"NOT START HERE!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:334
#: 8bb39d550e79459184ae5bac89b01846
msgid ""
"Multicopters have their whole own set of flight dynamics and structural "
"demands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:336
#: 052d3600851f458ab1f38879907c532c
msgid ""
"Until you have become experienced with them you stand virtually no chance"
" of designing and making a worthwhile MultiCopter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:338
#: 5523618521cd47049a90427c423ae974
msgid ""
"There is a really lovely QuadCopter design made by a newbie from bent "
"sheet aluminum on our site right now."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:340
#: e7285343a25a4baaa632e13269fdb524
msgid ""
"Unfortunately sheet aluminum is soft, the copter is heavy and hard "
"landings are common so a very bent copter is inevitable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:342
#: 7dd96d5664ad4661b7f55c5efe26c195
msgid ""
"Even if you are very experienced, you will certainly need to make several"
" copters before you achieve a worthwhile design."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:344
#: 2b7271fccdc4472f86be2a1e35fd292b
msgid ""
"I won't say Experts only, but you really need to go through at least 3 or"
" 4 commercial MultiCopters before you even think about doing this."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:347
#: 156e18b3a979424284182779e7fa71a8
msgid ""
"I have made over a dozen different CAD designs so far and have not yet "
"built one, I will make one, but I'm not ready yet and I know it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:351
#: a936ef8e589740f7be0c4c472a263cf3
msgid "Brand Name Ready to Fly"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:353
#: eaea764a66b2460284b107f1e7bc1ae8
msgid ""
"A few words about the **Brand Name** Ready To Fly QuadCopters like the "
"**Parrot**, the **DJI Phantom** and the **Blade 350QX**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:356
#: 3d18dc1f9af34200a04e24de43ba966e
msgid ""
"Within the scope of their capabilities these are generally well made and "
"often a reasonable bargain for what they do."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:358
#: ef566b6442254a7da4d0a2aff2d1a62d
msgid ""
"But they are also not easily modified or improved on and are not easy to "
"upgrade to a more powerful autopilot like the Pixhawk."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:360
#: 5f74ad0803ca4a7b8274fc3bb1af4352
msgid ""
"So although they are a moderately capable one stop solution, they can "
"also be a bit of a costly dead end."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:362
#: 7e184a034d144bc2891fd06d51d2c74d
msgid ""
"You can put together a **Flamewheel ARF kit** with a top end **Pixhawk "
"autopilot** for about the same money and be way ahead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:367
#: aef5a1dd01b443489165c6679806017b
msgid "Which Approach is Right for You"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:369
#: ad7350d756df46458358abf76b90817c
msgid ""
"It is very important to match your approach to your capability level, if "
"you overreach you can end up with a negative experience."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:371
#: 0b5a03df16014e96b9bbb076d30b1aab
msgid ""
"It is also much more important to take a robust and conservative approach"
" than to try to do everything the first time out."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:374
#: c75d17acd104474b9a70c7d77fd31368
msgid ""
"The simplest approach is to get a **Ready to Fly** system or an **All "
"Inclusive Kit**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:376
#: d046ed913eb9460397793207706fa1b9
msgid ""
"However, a good **Almost Ready To Fly** kit plus some carefully chosen "
"components can also result in an outstanding copter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:378
#: aa9c495c2579401c8a7cac37d6881438
msgid ""
"The ARF approach can often cost somewhat less and enable you to construct"
" a copter that is specifically tailored to your needs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:380
#: 0edb3618ff194e219e7c501b7a9e299f
msgid ""
"The **Frame Kit** approach presumes that you have sufficient knowledge to"
" specify appropriate components that will work together."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:383
#: 869c64c78192476293d07fb6bbe496c8
msgid ""
"But it does let you put together a copter that is specifically optimized "
"for your needs and desires."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:385
#: 56e3853b03eb4805b584be24f3a03d76
msgid ""
"Unless you find and scrupulously follow a comprehensive article detailing"
" a specific \"build\" a Frame Kit should not be your first copter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:388
#: 65a695106852433c846014d789edc3d4
msgid ""
"Clearly that goes double for **Scratch Built**. It isn't actually all "
"that hard to build a MultiCopter frame."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:390
#: ce52134377d24710bbfc954ef5d746e4
msgid ""
"But the overall process and component matching to make it work well is "
"really for the experienced MultiCopter operator / builder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:393
#: 557a6798f2194caea63a23882cf3dc9f
msgid ""
"There are expensive, high end Multicopters, which are generally oriented "
"to commercial photo or video use and outside our scope here."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:395
#: d86a9a66f2a74ce1a9cfe0de38d8d5e7
msgid ""
"All of the Copters I have and will be putting together incorporate a "
":ref:`Pixhawk <common-pixhawk-overview>` autopilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:398
#: d1997c04500f430fbf773552e9cdffc7
msgid ""
"These are the best and most capable autopilots available and they have "
"great **DIYDrones** community support."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:400
#: a1b553a998094a7e8085c8dcf19a40ee
msgid ""
"Beware of clones and counterfeits, they often have small differences that"
" end up making them completely unusable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/build-your-own-multicopter.rst:402
#: 6fbc7b99cdfc452fbec348f15a38cb1e
msgid ""
"Don't say I didn't warn you: \"Caveat Emptor\" and \"You get what you pay"
" for\"."
msgstr ""

